\b Note:
\b0  The APA-1460 SlimSCSI adapter is actively terminated by default and cannot be changed, as it is at the other physical end of the SCSI bus and both ends must be terminated.\
	
\b Note: 
\b0 The
\b  
\b0 APA-1460 SlimSCSI adapter does not provide term power; if a SCSI device connected to it requires term power output, make sure the device provides this output.\
	
\b Note: 
\b0 The
\b  
\b0 APA-1460 SlimSCSI adapter supports only single-ended SCSI devices. Differential SCSI devices may be damaged if connected to the host adapter bus.\
